<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>BurmillaOS</title><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/</link><description>Recent content on BurmillaOS</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><copyright>© 2020–2026 [BurmillaOS community](https://github.com/burmilla) · Documentation licensed under [Apache 2.0](https://github.com/burmilla/burmilla.github.io/blob/master/LICENSE)</copyright><atom:link href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title/><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-console/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-console/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="custom-console"&gt;Custom Console&lt;a class="anchor" href="#custom-console"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When &lt;a href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/workstation/boot-from-iso/"&gt;booting from the ISO&lt;/a&gt;, BurmillaOS starts with the &lt;code&gt;default&lt;/code&gt; console, which is based on &lt;a href="https://github.com/burmilla/os/blob/master/images/02-console/Dockerfile"&gt;&lt;code&gt;debian:trixie-slim&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (Debian 13) on BurmillaOS v3.0.x and on &lt;a href="https://github.com/burmilla/os/blob/v2.0.6/images/02-console/Dockerfile"&gt;&lt;code&gt;debian:bullseye-slim&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (Debian 11) on v2.0.x.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;No other console is officially supported.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="using-the-unofficial-custom-console-images"&gt;Using the unofficial custom console images&lt;a class="anchor" href="#using-the-unofficial-custom-console-images"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If you want to use other console, the most easy way is use the &lt;a href="https://github.com/benok/burmilla-os-console"&gt;unofficial custom console images&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To use this, you need to add the following settings to your cloud-init.yml.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;rancher:&#10; repositories:&#10; console:&#10; url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/benok/burmilla-os-console/master&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;With the settings above, you can select which console you want BurmillaOS to start with using the &lt;a href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/configuration/#cloud-config"&gt;cloud-config&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-kernels/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-kernels/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="custom-kernels"&gt;Custom Kernels&lt;a class="anchor" href="#custom-kernels"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kernel-version-in-burmillaos"&gt;Kernel version in BurmillaOS&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kernel-version-in-burmillaos"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;BurmillaOS basically uses the standard Linux kernel, but we maintain a kernel config ourselves. Due to various feature support and security fixes, we are constantly updating the kernel version.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;BurmillaOS&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Kernel&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;=v3.0.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;6.12.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;=v2.0.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;5.10.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;=v1.9.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;4.14.x&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="building-and-packaging-a-kernel-to-be-used-in-burmillaos"&gt;Building and Packaging a Kernel to be used in BurmillaOS&lt;a class="anchor" href="#building-and-packaging-a-kernel-to-be-used-in-burmillaos"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We build the kernel for BurmillaOS at the &lt;a href="https://github.com/burmilla/os-kernel"&gt;os-kernel repository&lt;/a&gt;. You can use this repository to help package your own custom kernel to be used in BurmillaOS.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Custom BurmillaOS ISO</title><link>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-burmillaos-iso/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-burmillaos-iso/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="custom-burmillaos-iso"&gt;Custom BurmillaOS ISO&lt;a class="anchor" href="#custom-burmillaos-iso"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s easy to build your own BurmillaOS ISO.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Create a clone of the main &lt;a href="https://github.com/burmilla/os"&gt;BurmillaOS repository&lt;/a&gt; to your local machine with a &lt;code&gt;git clone&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;$ git clone https://github.com/burmilla/os.git&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the root of the repository, the &amp;ldquo;General Configuration&amp;rdquo; section of &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile.dapper&lt;/code&gt; can be updated to use &lt;a href="https://burmillaos.org/docs/installation/custom-builds/custom-kernels/"&gt;custom kernels&lt;/a&gt;.&#10;After you&amp;rsquo;ve saved your edits, run &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt; in the root directory. After the build has completed, a &lt;code&gt;./dist/artifacts&lt;/code&gt; directory will be created with the custom built BurmillaOS release files.&#10;Build Requirements: &lt;code&gt;bash&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;docker&lt;/code&gt; (Docker version &amp;gt;= 1.10.3)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>